/// MethodBinding
///
/// Generic method resolution: locating a generic method on a receiver (inline /
/// inherent-impl / trait-impl / trait-default), solving its method-level type
/// params (turbofish or argument unification), stashing the solved bindings on
/// the call for the monomorphizer (`CallExprNode.resolved_type_args` - the frozen
/// contract), substituting a receiver's type-args into an abstract method return,
/// and reducing associated-type projections over a concrete base.
///
/// Env by pointer (arena/intern/ctx) + peers: `state` (symbolic_* + expected_type),
/// `types` (TypeUtils - type queries + DI lookups), `symbolic` (SymbolicChecker - 
/// param binding).  A fresh `TraitChecker` is constructed on demand (it is just a
/// 4-pointer view).
///
/// GATED (R1 - mono-after-sema): `resolve_method_return_with_explicit_args` and
/// `resolve_generic_method_return` carry `return fallback` pre-mono re-derivation
/// exits.  They are load-bearing while sema can still run before mono in some
/// paths, so they are kept and tagged; they become deletable (keep
/// only the symbolic-walk branch) once mono-after-sema fully lands.

namespace compiler::sema::method_binding;

